     "hq": "United States",
     "iso": "USA",
     "src": "cargill",
     "flag": "modeled",
     "metric": "Group revenue ~US$160bn (FY2024); the world's largest private agricultural trader; soy origination/crush a core segment.",
     "sourcing": [
      "BRA",
      "USA",
      "ARG",
      "PRY"
     ],
     "note": "One of the 'ABCD' traders. Major soybean origination and crushing in the US, Brazil and Argentina; large Brazil export-terminal footprint. Private, so per-commodity disclosure is limited.",
     "improve": "As a private company, Cargill's soy-specific volumes and deforestation exposure are opaque. It should publish bean-origination geography (Cerrado/Amazon vs. consolidated US), EUDR-traceability coverage, and crush-margin segment data so the market can size its exposure to the Brazil-China axis."
    },
